{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1795523383,"nonce":"YeYDVnj+EMsPxT0VQTlD0Yz6vUE=","title":"Build output fills the disk: target/ reached 58 GB","message":"The user cleared target/ at 58 GB on 2026-11-24. Measured from empty, nightly Cargo 1.100 (2026-08-22), M1 Pro:\n\n- `cargo test --workspace --no-run`: 8.6 GB in target/debug. 281 test binaries take 2.5 GB; blinc_recorder has 62 of them (1.6 GB), blinc_layout 61 (302 MB), blinc_cn 43 (253 MB). Each file under tests/ is its own binary and links its own copy of everything.\n- release-debug cn_demo plus cn_demo_costs: 6.0 GB. 1.9 GB of it was two copies of libblinc_app.a (blinc_app listed staticlib, so every build of it archived all of its dependencies, 950 MB each here and 254 MB in debug). Most of the rest was full DWARF.\n- With blinc_app an rlib only and release-debug at `debug = \"line-tables-only\"`: 1.9 GB, and the two builds took 3 min 10 s instead of 8 min 50 s. Time Profiler still shows inlined frames; inlined names lose their module path.\n\nWhy it grows: any change to features, profile settings, crate type or toolchain gives a unit and everything above it new hash folders under target/\u003cprofile\u003e/build/\u003cpkg\u003e/\u003chash\u003e, and the old ones stay. The crate-type change alone left 4.3 GB stale in target/debug. `cargo sweep` finds nothing in this layout. A sweep that runs the usual commands with `--message-format=json` and keeps only the folders they report removed the 4.3 GB, and the same commands then compiled nothing.\n\nRejected: `split-debuginfo = \"off\"` keeps no .o files (1.1 GB in target/debug) but drops line info for the binary's own code, and under LTO that is all of it.\n\nWork:\n1. blinc_app rlib only; release-debug line tables.\n2. A sweep tool in tools/.\n3. One integration test binary per crate for blinc_recorder, blinc_layout and blinc_cn.","files":null}]}